tions to the network - it must connect to an Ethereum node.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"For this purpose, every \",[\"$\",\"$L98\",null,{\"href\":\"/developers/docs/nodes-and-clients/#execution-clients\",\"children\":\"Ethereum client\"}],\" implements a \",[\"$\",\"$L98\",null,{\"href\":\"https://github.com/ethereum/execution-apis\",\"children\":\"JSON-RPC specification\"}],\", so there is a uniform set of methods that applications can rely on regardless of the specific node or client implementation.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L98\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.jsonrpc.org/specification\",\"children\":\"JSON-RPC\"}],\" is a stateless, light-weight remote procedure call (RPC) protocol. It defines several data structures and the rules around their processing. It is transport agnostic in that the concepts can be used within the same process, over sockets, over HTTP, or in many various message passing environments. It uses JSON (RFC 4627) as data format.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"client-implementations\",\"className\":\"group relative\",\"data-group\":true,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L1e\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute end-full flex h-full items-center opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-100 ease-in-out group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100\",\"aria-label\":\"client implementations permalink\",\"href\":\"#client-implementations\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L99\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"iconNode\":[[\"path\",{\"d\":\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\",\"key\":\"1cjeqo\"}],[\"path\",{\"d\":\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\",\"key\":\"19qd67\"}]],\"className\":\"lucide-link me-1 size-3\"}]}],\"Client implementations\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Ethereum clients each may utilize different programming languages when implementing the JSON-RPC specification. See individual \",[\"$\",\"$L98\",null,{\"href\":\"/developers/docs/nodes-and-clients/#execution-clients\",\"children\":\"client documentation\"}],\" for further details related to specific programming languages. We recommend checking the documentation of each client for the latest API support information.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"convenience-libraries\",\"className\":\"group relative\",\"data-group\":true,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L1e\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute end-full flex h-full items-center opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-100 ease-in-out group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100\",\"aria-label\":\"convenience libraries permalink\",\"href\":\"#convenience-libraries\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L99\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"iconNode\":\"$92:6:props:children:0:props:children:props:iconNode\",\"className\":\"lucide-link me-1 size-3\"}]}],\"Convenience Libraries\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"While you may choose to interact directly with Ethereum clients via the JSON-RPC API, there are often easier options for dapp developers. Many \",[\"$\",\"$L98\",null,{\"href\":\"/developers/docs/apis/javascript/#available-libraries\",\"children\":\"JavaScript\"}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"$L98\",null,{\"href\":\"/developers/docs/apis/backend/#available-libraries\",\"children\":\"backend API\"}],\" libraries exist to provide wrappers on top of the JSON-RPC API. With these libraries, developers can write intuitive, one-line methods in the programming language of their choice to initialize JSON-RPC requests (under the hood) that interact with Ethereum.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"consensus-clients\",\"className\":\"group relative\",\"data-group\":true,\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L1e\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute end-full flex h-full items-center opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-100 ease-in-out group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100\",\"aria-label\":\"consensus clients permalink\",\"href\":\"#consensus-clients\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L99\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"iconNode\":\"$92:6:pro